@flexiarg operator/say-a-continue-means-follow-the-path
@title Say That A Continue Means Follow The Path
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 4 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-4DmSW5 turn-GqW2Eb turn-Uy0DIA turn-nA7g22; first proposed for: The agent has a long path of work and will often stop to ask whether to go on.
@why [collaboration-coherence/determined-fork-proto-psr]

! conclusion: Treat the signal as the warrant to proceed along the path, and ask only when the path itself is unclear.

  + IF:
    The operator says in advance that his 'OK, please continue' means follow the path.

  + HOWEVER:
    A standing rule can be applied to a case it did not foresee.

  + THEN:
    Treat the signal as the warrant to proceed along the path, and ask only when the path itself is unclear.

  + BECAUSE:
    The operator states the warrant once, instead of the agent asking each time.
